i hate online early morning routines  [Music]  i mean honestly how did we even get here  how did we all decide that the key to  having a happier more productive life is  just pushing our waking time earlier and  earlier in the day why do i see for so  long youtubers who work from home  kind of pushing this idea that having a  four or five am  morning routine is the key to success  when the likes of bill gates mark  zuckerberg  or elon musk are waking up at a 8am  morning so being a night owl who has  tried to change this a lot in the past  myself  i just wanted to make the case for the  non-guru  non-morning person type of people who  like me have been made to feel as though  the reason that we are not achieving our  dreams  is simply because we are not conscious  when the sun rises the first thing i  want to say before this video starts  is that most of us do not have a choice  anyway on when to start our days  we might have a crazy commute or work  starts at a specific time or we have  kids or other people in the house  who are just waking us up so we have to  be up to get them ready for school or  something so this video is not targeted  towards those people  this video is targeted towards people  like me who are night owls and who are  constantly  being told that we need to wake up  earlier i don't think there's a single  week of my life where i'm not told that  it's ridiculous for me to wake up at 9  00 a.m  and i read this quote that said that the  story about the early bird  just shows that the worm should have  stayed in bed so yeah i thought in the  end of the day i would just make a video  with all the counter arguments to waking  up early  that um i just wanted to put out there  so here it goes i'll be touching upon  three points  self-respect biology and my personal  experience so  starting with self-respect i absolutely  love this quote which i'm going to read  which says ours is a culture where we  wear our ability to get by  on very little sleep as a kind of badge  of honor that symbolizes work ethic or  toughness or some other virtue  but really it's a total profound failure  of priorities  and self-respect now i absolutely love  this there are so many things of which  sleep is one in the productivity realm  that tend to be actually quite terrible  when  i think of them saying things like oh i  haven't managed to talk to my family in  three weeks or you  have no idea how little time i have for  myself or i only managed to sleep three  hours last night  i don't know why we say this in the way  that it kind of implies that we're such  put together and productive people but  actually if you've just done this to be  productive  it's actually quite sad and it feels as  though there's no self-respect there  rather than it being something  incredible i don't i genuinely don't  think that there should be a pride in  being productive or structured or  waking up early when it goes against  your natural instincts and needs i think  that there are cases when it is good  to kind of go against yourself in doing  these things and that's when you're  helping others or when you're staying up  for family  but to do it just to kind of achieve  work goals  just to me feels a bit weird and  unnecessary the second point i will i  hope will clarify this a bit more has to  do with biology and there is scientific  evidence which suggests that there are  two types of people according to our  body clocks the morning larks and the  night owls and this is probably because  when we were living in tribes  some people would have to stay awake to  kind of hold guard on everyone else and  the night owls are the descendants of  those who would kind of prefer to do the  night's  shift and the morning larks were the  people who would prefer to wake up early  and do that sort of shift so there are  definitely among us people who  very naturally will wake up at 4 am i'm  absolutely not saying that those people  don't exist  but there are also people who are more  productive at night time and find it  very difficult to wake up early in the  morning and yes there are times where  you actually have to work against your  body clock if you have to wake up to  feed a baby or if you have to  travel or if you're doing shift work you  obviously have to work against your  natural  biology but i do think that constantly  fighting against it is just  not healthy and this is where i get  frustrated because there is kind of a  mismatch between the biology and our  social conventions  so in biology it's perfectly acceptable  that about half of the people  would find it very difficult to wake up  early in the morning and would rather  stay up very late at night and wake up  late  and the other half of people would find  it very difficult to stay up late  because they want to sleep up early and  naturally wake up early in the morning  which is absolutely fine but i feel as  though in society for some reason we've  gotten to the point  where we've kind of agreed amongst  ourselves that anyone who stays up late  at night is obviously very lazy  and waking up late in the morning is  also very lazy and unproductive  while the other people who wake up early  in the morning are just  more productive than the others and this  has led to a whole bunch of night owls  like myself trying to  shift our morning routines so we can  also fit in with this  yes if you wake up early in the morning  you will work better and that's where i  want to go to my last and third point  which is experience i have personally  tried to reset my body clock so  many times and it is possible  temporarily i can like stay up very very  late one night and then i'll have to  sleep early the next morning so then i  can wake up a bit  earlier the next morning um so if i put  an alarm on let's say at 8 or 7 am it's  not going to be as painful  but this is very temporary i will always  as soon as i am semi well rested at some  point i will go back to wanting to stay  up late and wake up late my natural  makeup time  always resets towards 9am for many many  years i've tried to change it and it  just goes  right back there and not only this even  if i'm well rested and i wake up early  in the morning  i find that i don't do productive work  in the morning i like to take things  slow and i don't feel like working  while i'm the kind of person who in the  afternoon or the evening or night even  at 3am i can do very productive work  so i don't think there is literally any  sort of difference and i don't think  that we should be thinking that these  people who want to wake up early  or are waking early have some sort of  advantage or upper hand over us i know a  lot of morning people who wake up at 5  a.m  and by the time it is lunch time they've  done so much work well i've done nothing  but come 6 p.m or 7 p.m they are ready  to wrap it up and there's no way that  they can even start working and that's  where i begin  so i would say overall i don't think  that sleep really affects much i think  that  within your means if you're lucky enough  to kind of somehow design your life in a  way that you can sleep and wake up when  you want to  you should just follow and trust your  body rather than looking at youtubers  online or looking at other celebrities  and thinking that  the secret to their success or something  that affects their success is their  sleep or wake-up time  what works for other people might  definitely not work for you if you're  also  curious on learning more about sleep i'm  currently watching the signs of sleep  documentaries over on curiosity stream  which are  very kindly sponsoring this video also  next watch  is a documentary on dreams and how  dreams happen which i  am personally so interested in ever  since i discovered that not everyone can  lucid dream  dreams are something that i'm very very  curious about and i might actually  talk about in a video at some point if  you're interested but yes  for a price of a takeaway you can use my  discount code in the description to get  a full  year's worth of curiosity stream access  and also  you can get access to nebula where me  and other educational creators have our  videos up for an ad-free experience  so if you want to join me over there the  link is down below so yeah i'm just  genuinely very very passionate about  this topic because it comes up again and  again in my personal life and yeah i  would genuinely love to hear your  thoughts on the matter  have you also kind of struggled with the  judgment of other people for your  sleeping routines  and what do you think about this in  general if you haven't read the book why  we sleep  slightly problematic book but it's great  i would definitely recommend it and yeah  that was everything for me don't believe  everything you think and thanks  bye

